     "h": {
      "ar": "async def امتى؟",
      "en": "When async def?"
     },
     "p": {
      "ar": "FastAPI بيقبل `def` و`async def`. استخدم `async def` لما جوه الـ endpoint بتستنى حاجات async (زي `httpx.AsyncClient` اللي بينادي APIs تانية) — كده السيرفر يخدم طلبات تانية وهو مستني. لو الكود sync عادي (sqlite3 وpandas) سيبه `def` وFastAPI بيشغّله في thread لوحده. الغلطة الأخطر: كود sync بطيء جوه `async def` بيوقف السيرفر كله.",
      "en": "FastAPI accepts `def` and `async def`. Use `async def` when the endpoint awaits async things (like `httpx.AsyncClient` calling other APIs) — the server keeps serving others while it waits. For ordinary sync code (sqlite3, pandas) keep `def`, and FastAPI runs it in a thread for you. The worst mistake: slow sync code inside `async def`, which freezes the whole server."
     },
     "ex": "import asyncio, time\n\nasync def fake_api(n):          # stands in for: await client.get(url)\n    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n    return n * 10\n\nasync def main():\n    t = time.perf_counter()\n    results = await asyncio.gather(*(fake_api(n) for n in range(5)))   # 5 calls at the same time\n    print(results, f\"{time.perf_counter() - t:.1f}s instead of 5s\")\n\nasyncio.run(main())",
